Falsifies `system_tests::user::process_tests::each_member_of_a_process_has_its_own_current_cpu_page`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect, in milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one address space): a thread that joins a process is given a slot and a page, but the context
switch goes on publishing its core to the process's shared slot 0, so every member reads one
page, which §269 (how threads share a process) fork 6 refused.

Expected to fail: "a running member's page was never published", because the second member's own
page is never written.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs b/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
--- a/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/configure.rs
@@ -194,7 +194,8 @@ pub fn configure_thread_control_block_joining(
         }
         let bound = super::process::join(sched, tid, pid)?;
         let t = sched.threads.get_mut(tid).ok_or(abi::Error::NoSuchSlot)?;
-        t.space = Some(bound.with_current_cpu_page(kernel_va));
+        let _ = kernel_va;
+        t.space = Some(bound);
         t.thread_page = Some((space, slot));
         t.entry = (entry, user_sp);
         t.thread_pointer = thread_pointer;
